      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The indications to dissection of commissures in the algesic form of adhesive disease are determined. An experience with performing 36 laparoscopic operations is described. In 34 cases adhesiolysis was fulfilled under conditions of the I-III degree of the commissural process. Technical problems appeared while dissecting commissures in 2 patients with the IV degree of the commissural process due to pronounced dystopia of organs of the abdominal cavity. No complications were registered during operations. Control examination of 29 patients did not reveal recurrent diseases."},
